["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How Inconsistencies Between Multiple Conceptual Modeling Scripts Affect Readers’ Understanding","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-738542","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Software development process ambidexterity (SDPA) is the ability to demonstrate both process alignment and process adaptability simultaneously. Realizing process ambidexterity has recently been suggested as an effective approach to improving the performance of software development (SD) projects. To understand the mechanisms underlying the effects of ambidexterity, we focus in this study on the mediating effects of coordination, one of the most important activity in SD projects. Specifically, we hypothesize a mediating effect of coordination costs and coordination effectiveness on the relationship between SDPA and project performance. We conducted a quantitative study involving 104 SD projects across 10 firms to test the model. The results strongly suggest that the positive relationship between SDPA and project performance is negatively mediated by coordination costs and positively mediated by coordination effectiveness. We validate our research model with a case study in an organization employing several hundred IT professionals and derive several practical implications on this basis.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Werder, Karl","Li, Ye","Maedche, Alexander","Ramesh, Balasubramaniam"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-738535"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University","Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","University of Mannheim"],"keyword":["Ambidexterity","Coordination","Coordination cost","Cost effectiveness","Project performance","Software development"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"software development process ambidexterity and project performance a coordination cost effectiveness view","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85104682946","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-738535","identifier":[{"id":"85104682946","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-156b1e30-bd6e-4b86-a811-bb91549fce80"],"keyword":["Ambidexterity","coordination","coordination cost","cost-effectiveness","project performance","software development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-930BD7F65A44887E2373D2D8CB64AE19"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of mannheim","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Mannheim","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"karlsruhe institute of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karl","key":"werderpau","last":"Werder","locid":"b2431f12-bff1-4a97-af68-defe62b81aee","name":"Werder, Karl","orcid":"0000-0001-8481-1596","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ye","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Ye","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"maedchepau","last":"Maedche","name":"Maedche, Alexander","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Balasubramaniam","key":"rameshpau","last":"Ramesh","name":"Ramesh, Balasubramaniam","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tse.2019.2904571","issn":["00985589","19393520"],"issn_org":["00985589"],"journal":"IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Software Engineering"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-156b1e30-bd6e-4b86-a811-bb91549fce80"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Software Development Process Ambidexterity and Project Performance: A Coordination Cost-Effectiveness View.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-738535","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
